# Code example -- a REAL, runnable ggen consumer project that demonstrates
# THIS PACK'S OWN mechanism: point [packs] at readme-diataxis-pack via a
# local path (the exact, documented ecosystem convention in
# docs/how-to/consume-a-pack.md), give it a small real ontology.ttl subset
# of README facts, and `ggen sync run` it to watch the real Diataxis split
# happen. Not a disconnected toy -- the example demonstrates the pack by
# using the pack, the way any real ggen-marketplace consumer would.
# Three real files fanned out by templates/example-file.tmpl into
# examples/consume-readme-diataxis/.
<urn:readme-diataxis:example:000> a rdx:CodeExample ; rdx:position 0 ; rdx:exampleName "consume-readme-diataxis" ;
    dcterms:description "A real ggen consumer project that attaches readme-diataxis-pack via a local [packs] path and generates a live Diataxis doc set from a small ontology.ttl." .

<urn:readme-diataxis:example:000:ggen-toml> a rdx:ExampleFile ;
    rdx:forExample <urn:readme-diataxis:example:000> ; rdx:position 0 ;
    rdx:relPath "ggen.toml" ; rdx:language "toml" ;
    rdx:content """[project]
name = "consume-readme-diataxis-example"

[ontology]
source = "ontology.ttl"

[templates]
dir = "templates"

[packs]
readme-diataxis-pack = { path = "../ggen-marketplace/packs/readme-diataxis-pack" }
""" .

<urn:readme-diataxis:example:000:ontology-ttl> a rdx:ExampleFile ;
    rdx:forExample <urn:readme-diataxis:example:000> ; rdx:position 1 ;
    rdx:relPath "ontology.ttl" ; rdx:language "turtle" ;
    rdx:content """@prefix rdx: <https://seanchatmangpt.github.io/ggen-marketplace/readme-diataxis#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

# GENERATED by ggen from readme-diataxis-pack's rdx:ExampleFile
# urn:readme-diataxis:example:000:ontology-ttl. Edit that individual, not
# this file -- a re-sync overwrites it. Edit THIS file freely in your own
# copy of this example; it is your project's real ontology.

<urn:example:project> a rdx:Project ;
    dcterms:title "Example Project" ;
    dcterms:description "A minimal real project, admitted as RDF instead of README prose." ;
    rdx:license "MIT" .

<urn:example:run:000> a rdx:RunStep ; rdx:position 0 ; rdx:kind "clone" ;
    rdx:label "Clone the project" ; rdx:command "git clone https://example.invalid/example-project" .
<urn:example:run:001> a rdx:RunStep ; rdx:position 1 ; rdx:kind "install" ;
    rdx:label "Install dependencies" ; rdx:command "npm install" .

<urn:example:api:000> a rdx:ApiEndpoint ; rdx:position 0 ; rdx:method "GET" ; rdx:path "/health" ;
    dcterms:description "Liveness check." .

<urn:example:faq:000> a rdx:FaqEntry ; rdx:position 0 ;
    rdx:question "Why RDF instead of a README?" ;
    rdx:answer "So tutorial/how-to/reference/explanation content stays correctly separated as this project grows, instead of collapsing back into one flat file." .
""" .

<urn:readme-diataxis:example:000:readme-md> a rdx:ExampleFile ;
    rdx:forExample <urn:readme-diataxis:example:000> ; rdx:position 2 ;
    rdx:relPath "README.md" ; rdx:language "markdown" ;
    rdx:content """# consume-readme-diataxis example

A real ggen consumer project. `ggen.toml` attaches
[`readme-diataxis-pack`](../../../packs/readme-diataxis-pack/) by local
path, exactly as documented in
[`docs/how-to/consume-a-pack.md`](../../../docs/how-to/consume-a-pack.md).
`ontology.ttl` holds this project's own facts.

## Run it

```
ggen sync run
```

This generates a real `docs/` tree (`docs/index.md`,
`docs/tutorials/getting-started.md`, `docs/reference/api.md`,
`docs/explanation/faq.md`, ...) from `ontology.ttl`'s facts -- the same
mechanism this pack's own qualification fixture uses to generate its own
docs. Run it twice; the second run reports every file
`skipped: unchanged: content identical` -- replay is deterministic.

## Extend it

Add another `rdx:ApiEndpoint`, `rdx:FaqEntry`, or `rdx:RunStep`
individual to `ontology.ttl` and re-run `ggen sync run` -- the matching
doc file picks it up automatically, in the correct Diataxis quadrant.
""" .

# Playground -- a REAL, editable RDF fragment plus instructions to load it
# alongside the pack's own qualification fixture and watch a real doc
# regenerate. This is literally the mechanism this pack (and this whole
# ggen-marketplace session) is about: edit facts, re-run ggen sync,
# observe the deterministic projection change. Two real files fanned out
# by templates/playground-file.tmpl into playground/.
<urn:readme-diataxis:playground:000> a rdx:PlaygroundFile ; rdx:position 0 ;
    rdx:relPath "playground.ttl" ; rdx:language "turtle" ;
    rdx:content """@prefix rdx: <https://seanchatmangpt.github.io/ggen-marketplace/readme-diataxis#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

# GENERATED by ggen from readme-diataxis-pack's rdx:PlaygroundFile
# urn:readme-diataxis:playground:000. This is a scratch RDF fragment --
# edit it freely; a re-sync overwrites it back to this baseline.
#
# See playground/README.md for how to load this into a real consumer and
# watch docs/reference/api.md and docs/explanation/faq.md pick up your
# edits on the next `ggen sync run`.

<urn:playground:api:000> a rdx:ApiEndpoint ; rdx:position 90 ; rdx:method "POST" ;
    rdx:path "/api/playground" ; dcterms:description "Edit this endpoint, then re-run ggen sync run." .

<urn:playground:faq:000> a rdx:FaqEntry ; rdx:position 90 ;
    rdx:question "Can I try this myself?" ;
    rdx:answer "Yes -- edit this file, copy it into a real consumer's ontology.ttl (or append it to examples/consume-readme-diataxis/ontology.ttl), and re-run ggen sync run." .
""" .

<urn:readme-diataxis:playground:001> a rdx:PlaygroundFile ; rdx:position 1 ;
    rdx:relPath "README.md" ; rdx:language "markdown" ;
    rdx:content """# Playground

`playground.ttl` is a real, editable RDF fragment using this pack's own
`rdx:` vocabulary.

## Try it

1. Edit `playground.ttl` -- change the endpoint, add another
   `rdx:FaqEntry`, whatever you like.
2. Append its contents to
   [`examples/consume-readme-diataxis/ontology.ttl`](../examples/consume-readme-diataxis/ontology.ttl)
   (or point a fresh consumer's `[ontology] source` at this file
   directly).
3. Run `ggen sync run` from that consumer.
4. Check `docs/reference/api.md` and `docs/explanation/faq.md` -- your
   edit is there, in the correct Diataxis quadrant, deterministically.

This is the whole pattern this pack embodies: facts in RDF, doc structure
as a consequence, never hand-maintained.
""" .
